cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SemiSim 3D in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "SemiSim 3D: a 3-D drift-diffusion semiconductor device simulator"
type: software
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kot"
    given-names: "Mariusz"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kotmariusz/Semiconductor_devices_simulator"
abstract: >-
  A 3-D drift-diffusion simulator for semiconductor devices with a Python/Tk
  interface and a C (OpenMP) core: box method on graded rectangular or
  triangular-prism meshes, Scharfetter-Gummel fluxes, 47 device templates and
  a validation suite of 167 checks against closed-form theory.
keywords:
  - semiconductor device simulation
  - drift-diffusion
  - TCAD
  - finite volume method
  - Python
  - OpenMP
